# typescript
# ignore the generated JavaScript files
*.js.map
*.d.ts.map
# If you don't commit the compiled output, ignore the .js and .d.ts files in the same directory as the .ts source
# For most modern React/TS setups (like Vite, Create React App), this is handled by the build process, 
# so you usually only need to ignore the build output directory (/build or /dist) above. 
# The following lines are more relevant for a library setup where .js files might sit next to .ts files:
# *.js
# *.d.ts 

